        "id": "D026",
        "symbol": "L_Z",
        "type": "integral Chevalley Lie algebra",
        "definition": "L_Z is the free abelian group on the three abstract Chevalley generators, denoted x,y,h in the original problem, with Z-bilinear alternating bracket [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, [x,y]=h. In formulas for the action, the parameter endomorphisms x,y,h are the respective images of these generators; the integral Lie algebra is not defined as their possibly nonfaithful image in End_C(V).",
        "objects": [
          "x",
          "y",
          "h",
          "V"
        ],
        "binders": [],
        "depends_on": [],
        "requires": []
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/spec/definitions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "D027",
        "symbol": "L_K",
        "type": "K-Lie algebra",
        "definition": "L_K=L(K)=L_Z⊗_Z K=(Zx+Zy+Zh)⊗_Z K in the original Chevalley notation; bracket is extended K-bilinearly from the integral bracket. Its specified action on V_K is induced from the lattice restrictions of the three generators. This definition includes characteristic 2.",
        "objects": [
          "L_Z",
          "K",
          "V_K",
          "M"
        ],
        "binders": [],
        "depends_on": [
          "D026",
          "D006"
        ],
        "requires": []
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/spec/conclusion",
      "value": "V_K is nonzero, and for every K-linear subspace W of V_K invariant under the induced x,y,h operators, W={0} or W=V_K. Thus V_K is irreducible as a module for the stipulated Chevalley Lie algebra L_K."
    },
